---
{
  title: "cancelledp"
}
---
### NAME

    cancelledp() - Determine whether a promise settled because the body that
    owned it was cancelled. A cancellation carries a reason and unwinds like
    a rejection, but it is its own settlement, so rejectedp() does not
    report it.

### SYNOPSIS

    int cancelledp( promise p );

### DESCRIPTION

    Determine whether a promise settled because the body that owned it was
    cancelled. A cancellation carries a reason and unwinds like a rejection,
    but it is its own settlement, so rejectedp() does not report it.

    The cancellation is delivered to the body's next await, so a promise is
    still pending immediately after promise_cancel() returns; this reports 1
    only once the body has actually given up.

### PARAMETERS

    p  (promise)
       The promise to test.

### RETURN VALUES

    (int) 1 if the promise was cancelled, 0 if it is still pending or
    settled any other way.
